  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">uidetur,CVM NASCETVR NOMI-</l>
    <l n="2">NATIM HEREDEM VEL EXHE-</l>
    <l n="3">REDEM FACIO QVAMVIS, &amp;c.</l>
    <l n="4">Nam,ut ait Vlpianus L.3.§.1.D.de in-</l>
    <l n="5">iust.rupt. qui post testamentum factū</l>
    <l n="6">in uita nascuntur, ita demum per legē</l>
    <l n="7">Velleam rumpere testamentum pro-</l>
    <l n="8">hibētur,si nominatim sint exheredati.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Viuente patre.</i>) Vocem VIVENTE,</l>
    <l n="10">uacare,nemo non uidet.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Nascantur.</i>)Oratio postulat NASCA-</l>
    <l n="12">TVR. Mirum est autem, nullam ado-</l>
    <l n="13">ptiuorum à Sceuola interpositam esse</l>
    <l n="14">mentionem, quorum quasi agnatione</l>
    <l n="15">testamentum rupi constat, ex L.1, &amp;</l>
    <l n="16">8.D.de iniust.rupt. Sed ad hanc quo-</l>
    <l n="17">que formulam pertinere certum est,</l>
    <l n="18">nec testamentum ea formula commu-</l>
    <l n="19">nitum[?] eorum agnatione rumpi, quod</l>
    <l n="20">etiam maiori in re Papinianus confir-</l>
    <l n="21">mat L.Titio.23,in fin.D.de lib.&amp;post.</l>
    <l n="22" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Partitio.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Viuis nobis natos.</i>) Enunc.1. Vellea lex</l>
    <l n="24">eos qui testatore uiuo nascūtur, si uel</l>
    <l n="25">instituti uel exhæredati sint, rumpere</l>
    <l n="26">prohibet.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Videtur eos spectare.</i>) Sequitur 2. Prius</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The line break in "com.nu / nitum" is unclear; the word is read as commu-nitum with the second syllable doubtful. The running head letters after "IN L." are not fully legible and are read as GALLVS with doubt. No marginal notes are printed on this page.</notes>
